/* book Worked example: Q: A DSSS link sends Rb = 9.6 kb/s with a PN code at Rc = 1.2288 Mchip/s. (a) Find Gp as a ratio and in dB. (b) The demodulator needs Eb/N0 = 7 dB; find the jamming margin, ignoring losses, and say how much stronger than the signal a jammer may be.
   1. Gp = 1.2288 × 106/9.6 × 103 = 128 chips per bit.
   2. Gp(dB) = 10 log10 128 = 21.07 dB.
   3. Mj = 21.07 − 7 − 0 = 14.07 dB.
   4. As a ratio 101.407 = 25.5: the jammer may be about 25 times stronger than the signal at the antenna.
   Answer: Gp = 128 (21.07 dB); Mj = 14.07 dB, a jammer about 25.5 times the signal power. */
