/* book Worked example 2: Q: An FHSS radio sends 10 kb/s BFSK. It hops over a 25 MHz band in 25 kHz channels. Find the number of hop frequencies and the processing gain. For fast hopping at 4 hops per bit find the hop rate and dwell time; for slow hopping at 1000 hops/s find the bits per hop.
   1. N = 25 × 106/25 × 103 = 1000 channels.
   2. Gp ≈ N = 1000, which is 30 dB.
   3. Fast: hop rate = 4 × 10 000 = 40 000 hops/s; dwell = 1/40 000 = 25 µs per hop.
   4. Slow: bits per hop = 10 000/1000 = 10 bits; dwell 1 ms.
   Answer: 1000 hop frequencies, Gp = 30 dB; fast hopping 40 khop/s with 25 µs dwell; slow hopping 10 bits per hop. */
