/* book exam traps: The chip rate is not the bit rate: Rc = Gp × Rb. | Gains in cascade multiply as ratios, which is the same as adding their dB values; never add the ratios themselves. | Mj = Gp(dB) − (Eb/N0)req(dB) − Lsys; adding the required Eb/N0 instead of subtracting it is the common slip. The answer is a power ratio in dB, not watts. | Despreading needs the same code in step to within a fraction of a chip; a one-chip offset of an m-sequence gives a correlation of −1/N, almost nothing. | The chip-rate formula Rc/Rb is for DSSS. For FHSS the processing gain is the number of hop channels, Wss/B. */
