/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The delay spread is how long the echoes keep arriving: τmax from first to last, or the rms value στ.
   - Motion adds the time dimension.
   - Rayleigh, BPSK: Pb = ½[1 − √(γ̄/(1 + γ̄))] ≈ 1/(4γ̄)
   - γ̄ is the mean Eb/N0.
   - Diversity sends or receives the same bit over independently fading paths: different times (coding with interleaving), frequencies, or antennas.
   - Send N QAM symbols X[0] … X[N − 1] at the same time, each on its own subcarrier.
   - Δf is the subcarrier spacing in Hz.
   - H[k] is the channel's frequency response at subcarrier k and W[k] the noise.
   - The physical channel convolves the signal with its impulse response.
   - T = Tu + Tcp, Tcp ≥ τmax
*/
