/* book Worked example: Q: An OFDM system uses N = 64 subcarriers in 20 MHz, a 16-sample cyclic prefix and 64-QAM on every subcarrier. Find Δf, Tu, Tcp, T, the prefix overhead and the uncoded bit rate. Repeat the rate for 48 data subcarriers and rate-¾ coding, as in Wi-Fi.
   1. Δf = 20 MHz/64 = 312.5 kHz; Tu = 1/Δf = 3.2 µs.
   2. Sample time 1/(20 MHz) = 50 ns, so Tcp = 16 × 50 ns = 0.8 µs and T = 4.0 µs.
   3. Overhead Tcp/T = 0.8/4.0 = 20%.
   4. 64-QAM gives 6 bits per subcarrier: 64 × 6 = 384 bits per symbol, so R = 384/4.0 µs = 96 Mb/s.
   5. With 48 data subcarriers: 48 × 6 = 288 bits per symbol → 72 Mb/s; with rate-¾ coding 288 × 0.75/4.0 µs = 54 Mb/s.
   Answer: Δf = 312.5 kHz, Tu = 3.2 µs, Tcp = 0.8 µs, T = 4.0 µs, 20% overhead; 96 Mb/s uncoded on all 64, 54 Mb/s with 48 data subcarriers and rate-¾ coding. */
