/* book exam traps: Bit rates use T = Tu + Tcp, not Tu; the prefix is overhead. | OFDM removes ISI when Tcp ≥ τmax; it does not remove fading. Each subcarrier still has its own gain H[k]. | fd = vfc/c is the maximum Doppler shift; Tc ≈ 0.423/fd is a rule of thumb, and some books use 1/fd. State the rule you use. | A prefix exactly equal to the delay spread is enough; one even slightly shorter lets the previous symbol leak in. | Bits per OFDM symbol = (number of data subcarriers) × log2 M; forgetting either factor is common. */
